# Gluetun Monitor - Sites to test for VPN connectivity
# Add one URL per line
# Lines starting with # are comments; a "#" after whitespace starts an
# inline comment (https://example.com  # like this)
#
# All sites are tested in parallel. If any *critical* site fails consecutively
# (based on FAIL_THRESHOLD), Gluetun will be restarted. Sites are critical by
# default; see the role note below to make one advisory-only.
#
# Tips:
# - Use HTTPS sites for reliable connectivity testing
# - Include sites you actually need to reach through the VPN
# - Mix general sites with service-specific endpoints
# - More sites = more comprehensive testing (minimal overhead due to parallel execution)
#
# Per-URL tunables:
# - A slow-but-alive site can get its own probe timeout/retries with a
#   "|key=value" suffix, overriding the global TIMEOUT/WGET_TRIES for that URL only:
#       https://slow-api.example|timeout=25
#       https://flaky.example|timeout=20|tries=2
#   A bare URL (no "|") behaves exactly as before. Run the monitor with
#   --suggest-tunables to have it recommend these from observed history.
#
# Per-URL role (#110) — "|role=critical|advisory", default critical:
# - critical (default): its failure counts toward restarting Gluetun (today's behavior).
# - advisory: still probed and recorded for reachability, but its failure NEVER
#   restarts Gluetun. Use it for a site you want to watch that can't be reached
#   through the VPN regardless of tunnel health (e.g. geo-blocked from your exit) —
#   so it doesn't roll the tunnel pointlessly. If you stop caring about a site's
#   reachability entirely, just delete the line.
#       https://geo-blocked.example|role=advisory
#       https://slow-and-flaky.example|role=advisory|timeout=25

# General connectivity tests
https://www.google.com
https://cloudflare.com
https://1.1.1.1

